<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Bohatstvi fund H1 pretax lower.</title>
<headline>Czech Bohatstvi fund H1 pretax lower.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech investment fund IF Bohatstvi results for first-half 1997.</p>
<p>(millions of Czech crowns)</p>
<p> pre-tax profit (czk million)   79.675  vs    102.064</p>
<p> financial costs	     520.934  vs  2,791.520</p>
<p> financial earnings	  594.026  vs  2,896.382</p>
<p> basic capital	     1,255.527  vs  1,255.527</p>
<p> short-term obligations    244.182  vs  1,858.209</p>
<p> total assets		2,758.004  vs  3,387.044</p>
<p>Note. Full name is Investicni Fond Bohatstvi, managed by Prvni Investicni a.s. (PIAS), a unit of bank Investicni a Postovni Banka a.s.. IPB held a 25 percent share in the fund, according to the Central Securities Registry's latest update in the middle of July.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
